You can sort the array by the `id` property and then sum the `id` values using the `reduce` method. Here's how you can do it:

```typescript
function sortByAndSumIds(items: { id: number }[]): number {
  return items.sort((a, b) => a.id - b.id).reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.id, 0);
}

// Example usage:
const items = [{ id: 1 }, { id: 2 }, { id: 3 }];
console.log(sortByAndSumIds(items)); // Output: 6
```

This function first sorts the array of objects by the `id` property and then sums up all the `id` values.
